      {
        "id": "why",
        "widget": "acc",
        "label": "Why the tables are on the page",
        "body": "A widget's behaviour is a specification, and a specification nobody can see beside the thing is one nobody checks. Putting the table here makes a departure something you read rather than something you find.",
        "open": "false",
        "pos": 1
      },
      {
        "id": "what",
        "widget": "acc",
        "label": "What is checked, and how",
        "body": "Every row of every keystroke table is driven by a test that names it, and the run fails if a row is never driven. Every row of every attribute table names an element, and a second check asserts that element carries what the row says.",
        "open": "false",
        "pos": 2
      },
      {
        "id": "wont",
        "widget": "acc",
        "label": "What is not here",
        "body": "Every pattern that opens a surface over the page and moves focus into it: menu button, dialog, combobox, tooltip. They are the next thing to try, and half of one would say less than none.",
